:: Stall Upgrades
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "market">><<effects>>
<<run ensurePcStall()>>
You enter the small office responsible for the Connudatus market. A clerk behind the desk slides a catalogue of fittings and supplies across to you.
<br><br>
<<if $phase is "bought">>
	<span class="green">The clerk notes the order. It will be in place the next time you open your stall.</span>
	<br><br>
<<elseif $phase is "bags">>
	<span class="green">The clerk hands you the bags.</span>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<set $phase to 0>>
<<set _owned to setup.pcStall.upgrades.filter(u => pcStallHas(u.id))>>
<<if _owned.length gt 0>>
	Your stall has: <<print _owned.map(u => u.name).join(", ")>>.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<set _available to pcStallAvailable()>>
<<if _available.length gt 0>>
	<<for _p range _available>>
		<<capture _p>>
			<<if setup.inflation.canAfford(_p.cost, "marketStall")>>
				<<shopicon "register">><<link `"Buy the " + _p.name + " (" + formatMoney(setup.inflation.price(_p.cost)) + ")"` "Stall Upgrades">>
					<<money `-_p.cost` "marketStall">><<run pcStallBuy(_p.id)>><<set $phase to "bought">><</link>><<note `_p.note` "green">>
				<br>
			<<else>>
				<span class="grey">Buy the <<print _p.name>> (<<printprice _p.cost>>)</span><<note `_p.note` "grey">>
				<br>
			<</if>>
		<</capture>>
	<</for>>
<<else>>
	You own everything in the catalogue.
<</if>>
<br>
Paper bags make customers buy a little more. You give them away, one per sale.
You have <span class="gold"><<print $pcStall.bagsDisposable>></span>.
<br>
<<set _pack to setup.pcStall.disposablePack>>
<<if setup.inflation.canAfford(_pack.cost, "marketStall")>>
	<<shopicon "register">><<link `"Buy " + _pack.amount + " paper bags (" + formatMoney(setup.inflation.price(_pack.cost)) + ")"` "Stall Upgrades">>
		<<money `-_pack.cost` "marketStall">><<set $pcStall.bagsDisposable += _pack.amount>><<set $phase to "bags">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if pcStallHas("toteRack")>>
	<br>
	Tote bags make customers buy more than paper bags do. Customers pay you back what a tote costs, and returning customers sometimes bring their own. Totes are used before paper bags.
	You have <span class="gold"><<print $pcStall.bagsReusable>></span>.
	<br>
	<<set _toteCost to setup.pcStall.reusableCost * setup.pcStall.reusablePack>>
	<<if setup.inflation.canAfford(_toteCost, "marketStall")>>
		<<shopicon "register">><<link `"Buy " + setup.pcStall.reusablePack + " tote bags (" + formatMoney(setup.inflation.price(_toteCost)) + ")"` "Stall Upgrades">>
			<<money `-_toteCost` "marketStall">><<set $pcStall.bagsReusable += setup.pcStall.reusablePack>><<set $phase to "bags">><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<connudatusicon>><<link [[Leave|Connudatus Street]]>><</link>>
<br>
